From: gvwifi-los23 build kit
Subject: [PATCH] selinux: stop forcing permissive on gvwifi

Two bring-up shortcuts kept SELinux permissive no matter what userspace asked:
- CONFIG_SECURITY_SELINUX_PERMISSIVE makes fs/proc/cmdline.c inject
  androidboot.selinux=permissive into /proc/cmdline (so init stays permissive);
- sel_write_enforce() overwrote every write with new_value = 0.
Disable the config for gvwifi and restore upstream sel_write_enforce().
---
diff --git a/arch/arm64/configs/lineageos_gvwifi_defconfig b/arch/arm64/configs/lineageos_gvwifi_defconfig
index 9e190a9c..7965f0f0 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/configs/lineageos_gvwifi_defconfig
+++ b/arch/arm64/configs/lineageos_gvwifi_defconfig
@@ -3864,7 +3864,7 @@ CONFIG_SECURITY_NETWORK=y
 # CONFIG_SECURITY_PATH is not set
 CONFIG_LSM_MMAP_MIN_ADDR=4096
 CONFIG_SECURITY_SELINUX=y
-CONFIG_SECURITY_SELINUX_PERMISSIVE=y
+# CONFIG_SECURITY_SELINUX_PERMISSIVE is not set
 # CONFIG_SECURITY_SELINUX_BOOTPARAM is not set
 # CONFIG_SECURITY_SELINUX_DISABLE is not set
 CONFIG_SECURITY_SELINUX_DEVELOP=y
diff --git a/security/selinux/selinuxfs.c b/security/selinux/selinuxfs.c
index 1f09255a..e23931fe 100644
--- a/security/selinux/selinuxfs.c
+++ b/security/selinux/selinuxfs.c
@@ -184,7 +184,6 @@ static ssize_t sel_write_enforce(struct file *file, const char __user *buf,
 	selnl_notify_setenforce(new_value);
 	selinux_status_update_setenforce(new_value);
 #else
-	new_value = 0;
 	if (new_value != selinux_enforcing) {
 		length = task_has_security(current, SECURITY__SETENFORCE);
 		if (length)
